    "content": "Gary Woodland underwent successful surgery in September 2023 to remove a benign lesion (tumor) from his brain, which had caused fear and, later, severe PTSD. The procedure involved removing a baseball-sized portion of the tumor, and he returned to the PGA Tour in January 2024, later winning the 2026 Houston Open. Key Details of Gary Woodland's Surgery and Recovery: Procedure: Surgeons performed a craniotomy to remove a tumor that was causing neurological symptoms, such as fear and seizures. Post-Surgery Challenges: Following the surgery, Woodland struggled significantly with anxiety and PTSD, revealing in early 2026 that he often felt like he was \"dying\" and living in fear during his recovery. Comeback: Despite the mental challenges, Woodland continued to play, winning his first PGA Tour event since the surgery at the 2026 Texas Children’s Houston Open. Return to Play: He made his return to competitive golf at the Sony Open in January 2024. He has been open about his struggles to raise awareness and help others dealing with similar health battles.",
